#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# ops — the Operations board (FigJam) and its tiltak (Azure DevOps) in the terminal,
# with an innboks: type a line, Haiku sorts it into the right område/seksjon and adds
# what it knows (eier, frist, related open tiltak), and it goes back to the board as a
# sticky and/or to ADO as an Issue.
#
# Same board and conventions as the operations-referat / operations-nytt-referat skills
# in ~/visense/my-workday: newest «Referat <dato>» page, area Visense\Operations,
# tags operations-mote + rapportert:<dato> (+ «Ikke satt»), Due Date = neste møte.
#
# Type:
#
#   ops                      live view (TUI): 1 board · 2 tiltak · 3 innboks; n = nytt innspill
#   ops ls                   board and open tiltak, printed once
#   ops add "<tekst>"        classify one line and save it to the innboks (queued for the board)
#   ops sync                 write queued innboks entries to the board as stickies
#   ops ny [dato]            open the next meeting: clone the right template as «Referat <dato>»
#                            and carry the open tiltak forward in its tiltakslogg
#
# Stickies only go to a referat page for today or later: once a meeting is over, `ops ny`
# has to open the next one first (`ops sync --gammel` writes to the old page anyway).
# ADO Issues from the innboks are parented to the next meeting's epic, «Operations-møte
# <dato>», created as a stub if it doesn't exist yet; /operations-referat fills it in after.
#
# Reading the board needs a Figma personal access token (file_content:read), in
# FIGMA_TOKEN or the keychain:
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s figma-token -w '<figd_…>' -U
# Writing stickies goes through the Figma MCP server (`claude -p`, OPS_MODEL), which
# needs a one-time `/mcp` → figma → Authenticate in an interactive claude session.
# Without a token the board view is empty; tiltak and innboks still work.
#
# OPS_FIGMA_FILE overrides the board, OPS_MODEL the model (default haiku).
# TUI: 1/2/3 or tab view · ←→/hl column · ↑↓/jk card · enter details · n new · o open
#      · > / < move tiltak state · f queue · a ADO issue · S sync board · r refresh · q quit

